# Git workflow (mandatory)

## Branches

- `main` — production, deployed to Cloudflare Pages by the user. **Never push directly.**
- `dev` — integration, protected. **Never push directly.**
- `feature/<scope>-<slug>` — all agent work happens here.

## Required steps for every change

1. `git checkout dev && git pull origin dev`
2. `git checkout -b feature/<scope>-<slug>`
3. Implement, run `pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test -- --run`
4. `git add -A && git commit -m "<conventional-commits-message>"`
5. `git push -u origin feature/<scope>-<slug>`
6. `gh pr create --base dev --fill` using the PR template

## Conventional Commits

Use `type(scope): subject` — e.g. `feat(home): add hero section`, `fix(lint): drop unused import`, `chore(ci): bump node to 22`.

## Hard rules

- If you are unsure — STOP and ask before any git operation.
- Never run `git push --force`, `git reset --hard origin/...`, or rewrite history on shared branches.
- Never commit `.env*` files, secrets, or anything matching `*.key`/`*.pem`.
- Never check in `node_modules/`, `.next/`, `playwright-report/`, `test-results/`.
- One feature = one branch = one PR. Don't pile unrelated work into the same PR.
